#: ../../library/logging.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`!logging` --- Logging facility for Python"
msgstr ":mod:`!logging` --- Python 的日誌記錄工具"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:7
msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/logging/__init__.py`"
msgstr "**原始碼：**\\ :source:`Lib/logging/__init__.py`"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:13
msgid ""
"This page contains the API reference information. For tutorial information "
"and discussion of more advanced topics, see"
msgstr "此頁面包含 API 參考資訊。關於教學資訊及更進階主題的討論，請參閱"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:16
msgid ":ref:`Basic Tutorial <logging-basic-tutorial>`"
msgstr ":ref:`基礎教學 <logging-basic-tutorial>`"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:17
msgid ":ref:`Advanced Tutorial <logging-advanced-tutorial>`"
msgstr ":ref:`進階教學 <logging-advanced-tutorial>`"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:18
msgid ":ref:`Logging Cookbook <logging-cookbook>`"
msgstr ":ref:`日誌記錄手冊 <logging-cookbook>`"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:22
msgid ""
"This module defines functions and classes which implement a flexible event "
"logging system for applications and libraries."
msgstr ""
"這個模組定義了函式與類別 (class)，為應用程式和函式庫實作彈性的日誌管理系統。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:25
msgid ""
"The key benefit of having the logging API provided by a standard library "
"module is that all Python modules can participate in logging, so your "
"application log can include your own messages integrated with messages from "
"third-party modules."
msgstr ""
"由標準函式庫模組提供的日誌記錄 API 的主要好處是，所有的 Python 模組都能參與日"
"誌記錄，因此你的應用程式日誌可以包含你自己的訊息，並與來自第三方模組的訊息整"
"合在一起。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:30
msgid "Here's a simple example of idiomatic usage: ::"
msgstr "以下是慣用用法的簡單範例： ::"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:32
msgid ""
"# myapp.py\n"
"import logging\n"
"import mylib\n"
"logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n"
"\n"
"def main():\n"
"    logging.basicConfig(filename='myapp.log', level=logging.INFO)\n"
"    logger.info('Started')\n"
"    mylib.do_something()\n"
"    logger.info('Finished')\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"
msgstr ""
"# myapp.py\n"
"import logging\n"
"import mylib\n"
"logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n"
"\n"
"def main():\n"
"    logging.basicConfig(filename='myapp.log', level=logging.INFO)\n"
"    logger.info('Started')\n"
"    mylib.do_something()\n"
"    logger.info('Finished')\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:48
msgid ""
"# mylib.py\n"
"import logging\n"
"logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n"
"\n"
"def do_something():\n"
"    logger.info('Doing something')"
msgstr ""
"# mylib.py\n"
"import logging\n"
"logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n"
"\n"
"def do_something():\n"
"    logger.info('Doing something')"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:55
msgid "If you run *myapp.py*, you should see this in *myapp.log*:"
msgstr "如果你執行 *myapp.py*，應該會在 *myapp.log* 中看到："

#: ../../library/logging.rst:57
msgid ""
"INFO:__main__:Started\n"
"INFO:mylib:Doing something\n"
"INFO:__main__:Finished"
msgstr ""
"INFO:__main__:Started\n"
"INFO:mylib:Doing something\n"
"INFO:__main__:Finished"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:63
msgid ""
"The key feature of this idiomatic usage is that the majority of code is "
"simply creating a module level logger with ``getLogger(__name__)``, and "
"using that logger to do any needed logging. This is concise, while allowing "
"downstream code fine-grained control if needed. Logged messages to the "
"module-level logger get forwarded to handlers of loggers in higher-level "
"modules, all the way up to the highest-level logger known as the root "
"logger; this approach is known as hierarchical logging."
msgstr ""
"這種慣用用法的關鍵在於，大部分的程式碼只需使用 ``getLogger(__name__)`` 建立一"
"個模組層級的記錄器 (logger)，並使用該記錄器進行所需的日誌記錄。這種寫法很簡"
"潔，同時也讓下游程式碼在需要時能進行精細的控制。記錄到模組層級記錄器的訊息，"
"會被轉發給更高層級模組中記錄器的處理器 (handler)，一路往上直到最高層級、稱為"
"根記錄器 (root logger) 的記錄器；這種做法稱為階層式日誌記錄 (hierarchical "
"logging)。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:71
msgid ""
"For logging to be useful, it needs to be configured: setting the levels and "
"destinations for each logger, potentially changing how specific modules log, "
"often based on command-line arguments or application configuration. In most "
"cases, like the one above, only the root logger needs to be so configured, "
"since all the lower level loggers at module level eventually forward their "
"messages to its handlers.  :func:`~logging.basicConfig` provides a quick way "
"to configure the root logger that handles many use cases."
msgstr ""
"要讓日誌記錄發揮作用，就必須先設定它：為每個記錄器設定等級與目的地，也可能要"
"改變特定模組的記錄方式，這些通常會依據命令列引數或應用程式設定而定。在大多數"
"情況下，就像上面的例子，只有根記錄器需要這樣設定，因為所有位於模組層級、較低"
"層的記錄器最終都會將訊息轉發給根記錄器的處理器。:func:`~logging.basicConfig` "
"提供了一個快速設定根記錄器的方法，能應付許多使用情境。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:79
msgid ""
"The module provides a lot of functionality and flexibility.  If you are "
"unfamiliar with logging, the best way to get to grips with it is to view the "
"tutorials (**see the links above and on the right**)."
msgstr ""
"這個模組提供了很多的功能性以及彈性。如果你對於 logging 不熟悉，熟悉它最好的方"
"法就是去看教學（**請看右上方的連結**）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:83
msgid ""
"The basic classes defined by the module, together with their attributes and "
"methods, are listed in the sections below."
msgstr "此模組所定義的基本類別及其屬性與方法，列於以下各節。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:86
msgid "Loggers expose the interface that application code directly uses."
msgstr "記錄器公開應用程式程式碼直接使用的介面。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:87
msgid ""
"Handlers send the log records (created by loggers) to the appropriate "
"destination."
msgstr "處理器將（由記錄器建立的）日誌紀錄 (log record) 傳送到適當的目的地。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:89
msgid ""
"Filters provide a finer grained facility for determining which log records "
"to output."
msgstr "過濾器 (filter) 提供更精細的機制來決定要輸出哪些日誌紀錄。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:91
msgid "Formatters specify the layout of log records in the final output."
msgstr "格式化器 (formatter) 指定日誌紀錄在最終輸出中的格式。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:97
msgid "Logger Objects"
msgstr "Logger 物件"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:99
msgid ""
"Loggers have the following attributes and methods.  Note that Loggers should "
"*NEVER* be instantiated directly, but always through the module-level "
"function ``logging.getLogger(name)``.  Multiple calls to :func:`getLogger` "
"with the same name will always return a reference to the same Logger object."
msgstr ""
"記錄器具有以下屬性與方法。請注意，記錄器\\ *絕對不應該*\\ 被直接實例化，而應"
"一律透過模組層級函式 ``logging.getLogger(name)`` 取得。以相同名稱多次呼"
"叫 :func:`getLogger` 一律會回傳同一個 Logger 物件的參照。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:104
msgid ""
"The ``name`` is potentially a period-separated hierarchical value, like "
"``foo.bar.baz`` (though it could also be just plain ``foo``, for example). "
"Loggers that are further down in the hierarchical list are children of "
"loggers higher up in the list.  For example, given a logger with a name of "
"``foo``, loggers with names of ``foo.bar``, ``foo.bar.baz``, and ``foo.bam`` "
"are all descendants of ``foo``.  In addition, all loggers are descendants of "
"the root logger. The logger name hierarchy is analogous to the Python "
"package hierarchy, and identical to it if you organise your loggers on a per-"
"module basis using the recommended construction "
"``logging.getLogger(__name__)``.  That's because in a module, ``__name__`` "
"is the module's name in the Python package namespace."
msgstr ""
"``name`` 可能是以點號分隔的階層式值，例如 ``foo.bar.baz``\\ （不過也可以只是"
"單純的 ``foo``）。在階層串列中位置較低的記錄器，是位置較高之記錄器的子記錄"
"器。例如，對於名稱為 ``foo`` 的記錄器，名稱為 ``foo.bar``、``foo.bar.baz`` "
"和 ``foo.bam`` 的記錄器都是 ``foo`` 的後代。此外，所有記錄器都是根記錄器的後"
"代。記錄器名稱的階層類似於 Python 套件的階層；如果你使用建議的寫法 "
"``logging.getLogger(__name__)``，以模組為單位來組織記錄器，兩者就會完全相同。"
"這是因為在模組中，``__name__`` 就是該模組在 Python 套件命名空間中的名稱。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:120
msgid ""
"This is the logger's name, and is the value that was passed "
"to :func:`getLogger` to obtain the logger."
msgstr ""
"這是記錄器的名稱，也就是為了取得該記錄器而傳給 :func:`getLogger` 的值。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:123 ../../library/logging.rst:183
msgid "This attribute should be treated as read-only."
msgstr "此屬性應被視為唯讀。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:127
msgid "The threshold of this logger, as set by the :meth:`setLevel` method."
msgstr "此記錄器的門檻，由 :meth:`setLevel` 方法設定。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:129
msgid ""
"Do not set this attribute directly - always use :meth:`setLevel`, which has "
"checks for the level passed to it."
msgstr "請勿直接設定此屬性，請一律使用 :meth:`setLevel`，它會檢查傳入的等級。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:134
msgid ""
"The parent logger of this logger. It may change based on later instantiation "
"of loggers which are higher up in the namespace hierarchy."
msgstr ""
"此記錄器的父記錄器。它可能會因為之後實例化了在命名空間階層中位置更高的記錄器"
"而改變。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:137
msgid "This value should be treated as read-only."
msgstr "此值應被視為唯讀。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:141
msgid ""
"If this attribute evaluates to true, events logged to this logger will be "
"passed to the handlers of higher level (ancestor) loggers, in addition to "
"any handlers attached to this logger. Messages are passed directly to the "
"ancestor loggers' handlers - neither the level nor filters of the ancestor "
"loggers in question are considered."
msgstr ""
"如果此屬性求值為 true，記錄到此記錄器的事件除了會傳遞給附加在此記錄器上的所有"
"處理器之外，也會傳遞給更高層級（上層）記錄器的處理器。訊息會直接傳遞給上層記"
"錄器的處理器，而不會考慮這些上層記錄器的等級或過濾器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:147
msgid ""
"If this evaluates to false, logging messages are not passed to the handlers "
"of ancestor loggers."
msgstr "如果此屬性求值為 false，日誌訊息就不會被傳遞給上層記錄器的處理器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:150
msgid ""
"Spelling it out with an example: If the propagate attribute of the logger "
"named ``A.B.C`` evaluates to true, any event logged to ``A.B.C`` via a "
"method call such as ``logging.getLogger('A.B.C').error(...)`` will [subject "
"to passing that logger's level and filter settings] be passed in turn to any "
"handlers attached to loggers named ``A.B``, ``A`` and the root logger, after "
"first being passed to any handlers attached to ``A.B.C``. If any logger in "
"the chain ``A.B.C``, ``A.B``, ``A`` has its ``propagate`` attribute set to "
"false, then that is the last logger whose handlers are offered the event to "
"handle, and propagation stops at that point."
msgstr ""
"以一個例子具體說明：如果名為 ``A.B.C`` 的記錄器的 propagate 屬性求值為 true，"
"那麼透過像 ``logging.getLogger('A.B.C').error(...)`` 這樣的方法呼叫記錄到 "
"``A.B.C`` 的任何事件，會（在通過該記錄器的等級與過濾器設定的前提下）先傳遞給"
"附加在 ``A.B.C`` 上的所有處理器，接著依序傳遞給附加在名為 ``A.B``、``A`` 的記"
"錄器以及根記錄器上的所有處理器。如果 ``A.B.C``、``A.B``、``A`` 這條鏈中有任何"
"記錄器的 ``propagate`` 屬性被設為 false，那麼該記錄器就是最後一個將事件交給其"
"處理器處理的記錄器，傳播也會在此停止。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:159
msgid "The constructor sets this attribute to ``True``."
msgstr "此建構函式將該屬性設為 ``True``。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:161
msgid ""
"If you attach a handler to a logger *and* one or more of its ancestors, it "
"may emit the same record multiple times. In general, you should not need to "
"attach a handler to more than one logger - if you just attach it to the "
"appropriate logger which is highest in the logger hierarchy, then it will "
"see all events logged by all descendant loggers, provided that their "
"propagate setting is left set to ``True``. A common scenario is to attach "
"handlers only to the root logger, and to let propagation take care of the "
"rest."
msgstr ""
"如果你將處理器同時附加到某個記錄器\\ *以及*\\ 它的一個或多個上層記錄器，它可"
"能會多次發出同一筆紀錄。一般來說，你應該不需要將一個處理器附加到多個記錄器"
"上：只要將它附加到記錄器階層中位置最高的適當記錄器，它就能看到所有後代記錄器"
"所記錄的事件，前提是這些記錄器的 propagate 設定保持為 ``True``。常見的做法是"
"只將處理器附加到根記錄器，其餘的交給傳播機制處理。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:172
msgid "The list of handlers directly attached to this logger instance."
msgstr "直接附加到此記錄器實例的處理器串列。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:174
msgid ""
"This attribute should be treated as read-only; it is normally changed via "
"the :meth:`addHandler` and :meth:`removeHandler` methods, which use locks to "
"ensure thread-safe operation."
msgstr ""
"此屬性應被視為唯讀；它通常透過 :meth:`addHandler` 和 :meth:`removeHandler` 方"
"法來變更，這些方法會使用鎖來確保執行緒安全的操作。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:180
msgid ""
"This attribute disables handling of any events. It is set to ``False`` in "
"the initializer, and only changed by logging configuration code."
msgstr ""
"此屬性會停用所有事件的處理。它在初始化函式中被設為 ``False``，且只會由日誌設"
"定程式碼變更。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:187
msgid ""
"Sets the threshold for this logger to *level*. Logging messages which are "
"less severe than *level* will be ignored; logging messages which have "
"severity *level* or higher will be emitted by whichever handler or handlers "
"service this logger, unless a handler's level has been set to a higher "
"severity level than *level*."
msgstr ""
"將此記錄器的門檻設為 *level*。嚴重性低於 *level* 的日誌訊息會被忽略；嚴重性"
"為 *level* 或更高的日誌訊息，會由服務此記錄器的處理器發出，除非某個處理器的等"
"級已被設為比 *level* 更高的嚴重性等級。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:192
msgid ""
"When a logger is created, the level is set to :const:`NOTSET` (which causes "
"all messages to be processed when the logger is the root logger, or "
"delegation to the parent when the logger is a non-root logger). Note that "
"the root logger is created with level :const:`WARNING`."
msgstr ""
"建立記錄器時，等級會被設為 :const:`NOTSET`\\ （當該記錄器是根記錄器時，這會使"
"所有訊息都被處理；當該記錄器是非根記錄器時，則會委派給父記錄器）。請注意，根"
"記錄器是以等級 :const:`WARNING` 建立的。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:197
msgid ""
"The term 'delegation to the parent' means that if a logger has a level of "
"NOTSET, its chain of ancestor loggers is traversed until either an ancestor "
"with a level other than NOTSET is found, or the root is reached."
msgstr ""
"「委派給父記錄器」一詞的意思是：如果記錄器的等級為 NOTSET，就會沿著其上層記錄"
"器鏈往上走訪，直到找到等級不是 NOTSET 的上層記錄器，或是抵達根記錄器為止。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:201
msgid ""
"If an ancestor is found with a level other than NOTSET, then that ancestor's "
"level is treated as the effective level of the logger where the ancestor "
"search began, and is used to determine how a logging event is handled."
msgstr ""
"如果找到等級不是 NOTSET 的上層記錄器，該上層記錄器的等級就會被視為開始搜尋的"
"那個記錄器的有效等級 (effective level)，並用來決定如何處理日誌事件。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:205
msgid ""
"If the root is reached, and it has a level of NOTSET, then all messages will "
"be processed. Otherwise, the root's level will be used as the effective "
"level."
msgstr ""
"如果抵達根記錄器且其等級為 NOTSET，則所有訊息都會被處理。否則，會使用根記錄器"
"的等級作為有效等級。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:208 ../../library/logging.rst:552
msgid "See :ref:`levels` for a list of levels."
msgstr "等級清單請參閱\\ :ref:`levels`。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:210
msgid ""
"The *level* parameter now accepts a string representation of the level such "
"as 'INFO' as an alternative to the integer constants such as :const:`INFO`. "
"Note, however, that levels are internally stored as integers, and methods "
"such as e.g. :meth:`getEffectiveLevel` and :meth:`isEnabledFor` will return/"
"expect to be passed integers."
msgstr ""
"*level* 參數現在除了接受像 :const:`INFO` 這樣的整數常數外，也接受等級的字串表"
"示，例如 'INFO'。但請注意，等級在內部是以整數儲存，而"
"像 :meth:`getEffectiveLevel` 和 :meth:`isEnabledFor` 等方法會回傳整數，或預期"
"傳入的是整數。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:220
msgid ""
"Indicates if a message of severity *level* would be processed by this "
"logger. This method checks first the module-level level set by "
"``logging.disable(level)`` and then the logger's effective level as "
"determined by :meth:`getEffectiveLevel`."
msgstr ""
"指出嚴重性為 *level* 的訊息是否會被此記錄器處理。此方法會先檢查由 "
"``logging.disable(level)`` 設定的模組層級等級，再檢查"
"由 :meth:`getEffectiveLevel` 決定的記錄器有效等級。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:228
msgid ""
"Indicates the effective level for this logger. If a value other "
"than :const:`NOTSET` has been set using :meth:`setLevel`, it is returned. "
"Otherwise, the hierarchy is traversed towards the root until a value other "
"than :const:`NOTSET` is found, and that value is returned. The value "
"returned is an integer, typically one "
"of :const:`logging.DEBUG`, :const:`logging.INFO` etc."
msgstr ""
"指出此記錄器的有效等級。如果已使用 :meth:`setLevel` 設定了 :const:`NOTSET` 以"
"外的值，就回傳該值。否則，會沿著階層往根部走訪，直到找到 :const:`NOTSET` 以外"
"的值，並回傳該值。回傳值是整數，通常"
"是 :const:`logging.DEBUG`、:const:`logging.INFO` 等其中之一。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:238
msgid ""
"Returns a logger which is a descendant to this logger, as determined by the "
"suffix. Thus, ``logging.getLogger('abc').getChild('def.ghi')`` would return "
"the same logger as would be returned by "
"``logging.getLogger('abc.def.ghi')``. This is a convenience method, useful "
"when the parent logger is named using e.g. ``__name__`` rather than a "
"literal string."
msgstr ""
"回傳此記錄器的一個後代記錄器，由後綴決定。因此，"
"``logging.getLogger('abc').getChild('def.ghi')`` 回傳的記錄器會與 "
"``logging.getLogger('abc.def.ghi')`` 回傳的相同。這是個便利方法，在父記錄器是"
"以例如 ``__name__`` 而非字串字面值命名時很有用。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:249
msgid ""
"Returns a set of loggers which are immediate children of this logger. So for "
"example ``logging.getLogger().getChildren()`` might return a set containing "
"loggers named ``foo`` and ``bar``, but a logger named ``foo.bar`` wouldn't "
"be included in the set. Likewise, ``logging.getLogger('foo').getChildren()`` "
"might return a set including a logger named ``foo.bar``, but it wouldn't "
"include one named ``foo.bar.baz``."
msgstr ""
"回傳由此記錄器的直接子記錄器所組成的集合。舉例來說，"
"``logging.getLogger().getChildren()`` 可能會回傳一個包含名為 ``foo`` 和 "
"``bar`` 之記錄器的集合，但名為 ``foo.bar`` 的記錄器不會包含在該集合中。同樣"
"地，``logging.getLogger('foo').getChildren()`` 可能會回傳一個包含名為 "
"``foo.bar`` 之記錄器的集合，但不會包含名為 ``foo.bar.baz`` 的記錄器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:261
msgid ""
"Logs a message with level :const:`DEBUG` on this logger. The *msg* is the "
"message format string, and the *args* are the arguments which are merged "
"into *msg* using the string formatting operator. (Note that this means that "
"you can use keywords in the format string, together with a single dictionary "
"argument.) No % formatting operation is performed on *msg* when no *args* "
"are supplied."
msgstr ""
"在此記錄器上記錄一則等級為 :const:`DEBUG` 的訊息。*msg* 是訊息格式字串，"
"*args* 則是使用字串格式化運算子合併到 *msg* 中的引數。（請注意，這表示你可以"
"在格式字串中使用關鍵字，並搭配單一的字典引數。）若未提供 *args*，則不會對 "
"*msg* 執行 % 格式化操作。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:267
msgid ""
"There are four keyword arguments in *kwargs* which are inspected: "
"*exc_info*, *stack_info*, *stacklevel* and *extra*."
msgstr ""
"*kwargs* 中有四個會被檢查的關鍵字引數：*exc_info*、*stack_info*、"
"*stacklevel* 和 *extra*。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:270
msgid ""
"If *exc_info* does not evaluate as false, it causes exception information to "
"be added to the logging message. If an exception tuple (in the format "
"returned by :func:`sys.exc_info`) or an exception instance is provided, it "
"is used; otherwise, :func:`sys.exc_info` is called to get the exception "
"information."
msgstr ""
"如果 *exc_info* 求值不為 false，就會將例外資訊加入日誌訊息中。如果提供的是例"
"外元組（格式與 :func:`sys.exc_info` 的回傳值相同）或例外實例，就會使用它；否"
"則會呼叫 :func:`sys.exc_info` 來取得例外資訊。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:275
msgid ""
"The second optional keyword argument is *stack_info*, which defaults to "
"``False``. If true, stack information is added to the logging message, "
"including the actual logging call. Note that this is not the same stack "
"information as that displayed through specifying *exc_info*: The former is "
"stack frames from the bottom of the stack up to the logging call in the "
"current thread, whereas the latter is information about stack frames which "
"have been unwound, following an exception, while searching for exception "
"handlers."
msgstr ""
"第二個可選的關鍵字引數是 *stack_info*，預設為 ``False``。若為 true，就會將堆"
"疊資訊加入日誌訊息中，其中包含實際的日誌記錄呼叫。請注意，這與指定 "
"*exc_info* 時所顯示的堆疊資訊不同：前者是目前執行緒中從堆疊底部到日誌記錄呼叫"
"為止的堆疊框，而後者則是在例外發生後、搜尋例外處理程式的過程中已被展開 "
"(unwound) 的堆疊框資訊。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:284
msgid ""
"You can specify *stack_info* independently of *exc_info*, e.g. to just show "
"how you got to a certain point in your code, even when no exceptions were "
"raised. The stack frames are printed following a header line which says:"
msgstr ""
"你可以獨立於 *exc_info* 指定 *stack_info*，例如只是想顯示程式碼是如何執行到某"
"個位置的，即使沒有引發任何例外也可以。堆疊框會印在下面這行標頭之後："

#: ../../library/logging.rst:288
msgid "Stack (most recent call last):"
msgstr "Stack (most recent call last):"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:292
msgid ""
"This mimics the ``Traceback (most recent call last):`` which is used when "
"displaying exception frames."
msgstr ""
"這是模仿顯示例外堆疊框時所使用的 ``Traceback (most recent call last):``。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:295
msgid ""
"The third optional keyword argument is *stacklevel*, which defaults to "
"``1``. If greater than 1, the corresponding number of stack frames are "
"skipped when computing the line number and function name set in "
"the :class:`LogRecord` created for the logging event. This can be used in "
"logging helpers so that the function name, filename and line number recorded "
"are not the information for the helper function/method, but rather its "
"caller. The name of this parameter mirrors the equivalent one in "
"the :mod:`warnings` module."
msgstr ""
"第三個可選的關鍵字引數是 *stacklevel*，預設為 ``1``。若大於 1，則在計算為該日"
"誌事件所建立的 :class:`LogRecord` 中所設定的列號和函式名稱時，會略過相應數量"
"的堆疊框。這可用於日誌記錄輔助函式中，讓所記錄的函式名稱、檔案名稱和列號不是"
"輔助函式／方法本身的資訊，而是其呼叫者的資訊。此參數的名稱與 :mod:`warnings` "
"模組中對應的參數相同。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:303
msgid ""
"The fourth keyword argument is *extra* which can be used to pass a "
"dictionary which is used to populate the :attr:`~object.__dict__` of "
"the :class:`LogRecord` created for the logging event with user-defined "
"attributes. These custom attributes can then be used as you like. For "
"example, they could be incorporated into logged messages. For example::"
msgstr ""
"第四個關鍵字引數是 *extra*，可用來傳遞一個字典，以使用者定義的屬性填入為該日"
"誌事件所建立之 :class:`LogRecord` 的 :attr:`~object.__dict__`。之後你就可以隨"
"意使用這些自訂屬性，例如將它們併入所記錄的訊息中。例如： ::"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:310
msgid ""
"FORMAT = '%(asctime)s %(clientip)-15s %(user)-8s %(message)s'\n"
"logging.basicConfig(format=FORMAT)\n"
"d = {'clientip': '192.168.0.1', 'user': 'fbloggs'}\n"
"logger = logging.getLogger('tcpserver')\n"
"logger.warning('Protocol problem: %s', 'connection reset', extra=d)"
msgstr ""
"FORMAT = '%(asctime)s %(clientip)-15s %(user)-8s %(message)s'\n"
"logging.basicConfig(format=FORMAT)\n"
"d = {'clientip': '192.168.0.1', 'user': 'fbloggs'}\n"
"logger = logging.getLogger('tcpserver')\n"
"logger.warning('Protocol problem: %s', 'connection reset', extra=d)"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:316
msgid "would print something like"
msgstr "會印出類似以下的內容"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:318
msgid ""
"2006-02-08 22:20:02,165 192.168.0.1 fbloggs  Protocol problem: connection "
"reset"
msgstr ""
"2006-02-08 22:20:02,165 192.168.0.1 fbloggs  Protocol problem: connection "
"reset"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:322
msgid ""
"The keys in the dictionary passed in *extra* should not clash with the keys "
"used by the logging system. (See the section on :ref:`logrecord-attributes` "
"for more information on which keys are used by the logging system.)"
msgstr ""
"*extra* 中傳入的字典，其鍵不應與日誌記錄系統所使用的鍵衝突。（關於日誌記錄系"
"統會使用哪些鍵，詳見 :ref:`logrecord-attributes`。）"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:326
msgid ""
"If you choose to use these attributes in logged messages, you need to "
"exercise some care. In the above example, for instance, "
"the :class:`Formatter` has been set up with a format string which expects "
"'clientip' and 'user' in the attribute dictionary of the :class:`LogRecord`. "
"If these are missing, the message will not be logged because a string "
"formatting exception will occur. So in this case, you always need to pass "
"the *extra* dictionary with these keys."
msgstr ""
"如果你選擇在記錄的訊息中使用這些屬性，就需要多加小心。例如在上面的範例"
"中，:class:`Formatter` 已設定了一個格式字串，預期 :class:`LogRecord` 的屬性字"
"典中有 'clientip' 和 'user'。如果缺少這些鍵，訊息就不會被記錄，因為會發生字串"
"格式化例外。所以在這種情況下，你必須一律傳入帶有這些鍵的 *extra* 字典。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:333
msgid ""
"While this might be annoying, this feature is intended for use in "
"specialized circumstances, such as multi-threaded servers where the same "
"code executes in many contexts, and interesting conditions which arise are "
"dependent on this context (such as remote client IP address and "
"authenticated user name, in the above example). In such circumstances, it is "
"likely that specialized :class:`Formatter`\\ s would be used with "
"particular :class:`Handler`\\ s."
msgstr ""
"雖然這可能有點麻煩，但此功能是為特殊情況而設計的，例如在多執行緒伺服器中，同"
"一段程式碼會在許多情境下執行，而值得關注的狀況取決於該情境（例如上面範例中的"
"遠端用戶端 IP 位址和已驗證的使用者名稱）。在這種情況下，特製"
"的 :class:`Formatter` 很可能會搭配特定的 :class:`Handler` 使用。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:340
msgid ""
"If no handler is attached to this logger (or any of its ancestors, taking "
"into account the relevant :attr:`Logger.propagate` attributes), the message "
"will be sent to the handler set on :data:`lastResort`."
msgstr ""
"如果此記錄器（或考量相關 :attr:`Logger.propagate` 屬性後的任何上層記錄器）沒"
"有附加任何處理器，訊息將會被傳送到 :data:`lastResort` 上所設定的處理器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:344
msgid "The *stack_info* parameter was added."
msgstr "新增 *stack_info* 參數。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:347
msgid "The *exc_info* parameter can now accept exception instances."
msgstr "*exc_info* 參數現在可以接受例外實例。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:350
msgid "The *stacklevel* parameter was added."
msgstr "新增 *stacklevel* 參數。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:356
msgid ""
"Logs a message with level :const:`INFO` on this logger. The arguments are "
"interpreted as for :meth:`debug`."
msgstr ""
"在此記錄器上記錄一則等級為 :const:`INFO` 的訊息。引數的解讀方式"
"與 :meth:`debug` 相同。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:362
msgid ""
"Logs a message with level :const:`WARNING` on this logger. The arguments are "
"interpreted as for :meth:`debug`."
msgstr ""
"在此記錄器上記錄一則等級為 :const:`WARNING` 的訊息。引數的解讀方式"
"與 :meth:`debug` 相同。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:365
msgid ""
"There is an obsolete method ``warn`` which is functionally identical to "
"``warning``. As ``warn`` is deprecated, please do not use it - use "
"``warning`` instead."
msgstr ""
"有一個已過時的方法 ``warn``，其功能與 ``warning`` 完全相同。由於 ``warn`` 已"
"被棄用，請不要使用它，請改用 ``warning``。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:371
msgid ""
"Logs a message with level :const:`ERROR` on this logger. The arguments are "
"interpreted as for :meth:`debug`."
msgstr ""
"在此記錄器上記錄一則等級為 :const:`ERROR` 的訊息。引數的解讀方式"
"與 :meth:`debug` 相同。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:377
msgid ""
"Logs a message with level :const:`CRITICAL` on this logger. The arguments "
"are interpreted as for :meth:`debug`."
msgstr ""
"在此記錄器上記錄一則等級為 :const:`CRITICAL` 的訊息。引數的解讀方式"
"與 :meth:`debug` 相同。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:383
msgid ""
"Logs a message with integer level *level* on this logger. The other "
"arguments are interpreted as for :meth:`debug`."
msgstr ""
"在此記錄器上記錄一則整數等級為 *level* 的訊息。其他引數的解讀方式"
"與 :meth:`debug` 相同。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:389
msgid ""
"Logs a message with level :const:`ERROR` on this logger. The arguments are "
"interpreted as for :meth:`debug`. Exception info is added to the logging "
"message. This method should only be called from an exception handler."
msgstr ""
"在此記錄器上記錄一則等級為 :const:`ERROR` 的訊息。引數的解讀方式"
"與 :meth:`debug` 相同。例外資訊會被加入日誌訊息中。此方法只應從例外處理程式中"
"呼叫。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:396
msgid "Adds the specified filter *filter* to this logger."
msgstr "將指定的過濾器 *filter* 加入此記錄器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:401
msgid "Removes the specified filter *filter* from this logger."
msgstr "從此記錄器移除指定的過濾器 *filter*。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:406
msgid ""
"Apply this logger's filters to the record and return ``True`` if the record "
"is to be processed. The filters are consulted in turn, until one of them "
"returns a false value. If none of them return a false value, the record will "
"be processed (passed to handlers). If one returns a false value, no further "
"processing of the record occurs."
msgstr ""
"將此記錄器的過濾器套用到紀錄上，若該紀錄要被處理則回傳 ``True``。過濾器會依序"
"被詢問，直到其中一個回傳假值為止。如果沒有任何過濾器回傳假值，該紀錄就會被處"
"理（傳遞給處理器）。如果有一個回傳假值，就不會再對該紀錄進行任何處理。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:415
msgid "Adds the specified handler *hdlr* to this logger."
msgstr "將指定的處理器 *hdlr* 加入此記錄器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:420
msgid "Removes the specified handler *hdlr* from this logger."
msgstr "從此記錄器移除指定的處理器 *hdlr*。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:425
msgid ""
"Finds the caller's source filename and line number. Returns the filename, "
"line number, function name and stack information as a 4-element tuple. The "
"stack information is returned as ``None`` unless *stack_info* is ``True``."
msgstr ""
"找出呼叫者的原始檔案名稱和列號。以一個 4 元素的元組回傳檔案名稱、列號、函式名"
"稱和堆疊資訊。除非 *stack_info* 為 ``True``，否則堆疊資訊會以 ``None`` 回傳。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:429
msgid ""
"The *stacklevel* parameter is passed from code calling the :meth:`debug` and "
"other APIs. If greater than 1, the excess is used to skip stack frames "
"before determining the values to be returned. This will generally be useful "
"when calling logging APIs from helper/wrapper code, so that the information "
"in the event log refers not to the helper/wrapper code, but to the code that "
"calls it."
msgstr ""
"*stacklevel* 參數是由呼叫 :meth:`debug` 及其他 API 的程式碼傳入的。若大於 1，"
"超出的部分會用來在決定要回傳的值之前略過堆疊框。從輔助／包裝程式碼呼叫日誌記"
"錄 API 時，這通常很有用，如此一來，事件日誌中的資訊所指的就不是輔助／包裝程式"
"碼，而是呼叫它的程式碼。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:439
msgid ""
"Handles a record by passing it to all handlers associated with this logger "
"and its ancestors (until a false value of *propagate* is found). This method "
"is used for unpickled records received from a socket, as well as those "
"created locally. Logger-level filtering is applied "
"using :meth:`~Logger.filter`."
msgstr ""
"透過將紀錄傳遞給與此記錄器及其上層記錄器關聯的所有處理器（直到遇到 "
"*propagate* 為假值為止）來處理該紀錄。此方法用於從 socket 接收並經 unpickle "
"的紀錄，也用於在本地建立的紀錄。記錄器層級的過濾是使"
"用 :meth:`~Logger.filter` 來套用的。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:447
msgid ""
"This is a factory method which can be overridden in subclasses to create "
"specialized :class:`LogRecord` instances."
msgstr ""
"這是一個工廠方法，可以在子類別中覆寫，以建立特製的 :class:`LogRecord` 實例。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:452
msgid ""
"Checks to see if this logger has any handlers configured. This is done by "
"looking for handlers in this logger and its parents in the logger hierarchy. "
"Returns ``True`` if a handler was found, else ``False``. The method stops "
"searching up the hierarchy whenever a logger with the 'propagate' attribute "
"set to false is found - that will be the last logger which is checked for "
"the existence of handlers."
msgstr ""
"檢查此記錄器是否設定了任何處理器。做法是在記錄器階層中尋找此記錄器及其上層記"
"錄器的處理器。如果找到處理器就回傳 ``True``，否則回傳 ``False``。每當遇到 "
"'propagate' 屬性被設為 false 的記錄器時，此方法就會停止往上搜尋階層，該記錄器"
"就是最後一個被檢查是否有處理器的記錄器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:461
msgid "Loggers can now be pickled and unpickled."
msgstr "記錄器現在可以被 pickle 和 unpickle。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:467
msgid "Logging Levels"
msgstr "日誌等級"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:469
msgid ""
"The numeric values of logging levels are given in the following table. These "
"are primarily of interest if you want to define your own levels, and need "
"them to have specific values relative to the predefined levels. If you "
"define a level with the same numeric value, it overwrites the predefined "
"value; the predefined name is lost."
msgstr ""
"日誌等級的數值如下表所示。這些數值主要在你想定義自己的等級，並需要它們相對於"
"預定義等級具有特定值時才需要關注。如果你定義的等級與某個預定義等級的數值相"
"同，它會覆寫該預定義的值；預定義的名稱也會因此消失。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:476
msgid "Level"
msgstr "等級"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:476
msgid "Numeric value"
msgstr "數值"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:476
msgid "What it means / When to use it"
msgstr "代表意義／使用時機"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:478
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:478
msgid ""
"When set on a logger, indicates that ancestor loggers are to be consulted to "
"determine the effective level. If that still resolves to :const:`!NOTSET`, "
"then all events are logged. When set on a handler, all events are handled."
msgstr ""
"設定在記錄器上時，表示要查詢上層記錄器來決定有效等級。如果結果仍然"
"是 :const:`!NOTSET`，則所有事件都會被記錄。設定在處理器上時，所有事件都會被處"
"理。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:486
msgid "10"
msgstr "10"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:486
msgid ""
"Detailed information, typically only of interest to a developer trying to "
"diagnose a problem."
msgstr "詳細的資訊，通常只有試圖診斷問題的開發者才會需要。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:490
msgid "20"
msgstr "20"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:490
msgid "Confirmation that things are working as expected."
msgstr "確認一切都按預期運作。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:493
msgid "30"
msgstr "30"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:493
msgid ""
"An indication that something unexpected happened, or that a problem might "
"occur in the near future (e.g. 'disk space low'). The software is still "
"working as expected."
msgstr ""
"表示發生了非預期的事情，或近期可能會出現問題（例如「磁碟空間不足」）。軟體仍"
"按預期運作。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:500
msgid "40"
msgstr "40"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:500
msgid ""
"Due to a more serious problem, the software has not been able to perform "
"some function."
msgstr "因為有更嚴重的問題，軟體無法執行某些功能。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:504
msgid "50"
msgstr "50"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:504
msgid ""
"A serious error, indicating that the program itself may be unable to "
"continue running."
msgstr "嚴重錯誤，表示此程式本身可能無法繼續執行。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:513
msgid "Handler Objects"
msgstr "Handler 物件"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:515
msgid ""
"Handlers have the following attributes and methods. Note "
"that :class:`Handler` is never instantiated directly; this class acts as a "
"base for more useful subclasses. However, the :meth:`!__init__` method in "
"subclasses needs to call :meth:`Handler.__init__`."
msgstr ""
"處理器具有以下屬性與方法。請注意，:class:`Handler` 從不直接實例化；此類別是作"
"為更實用之子類別的基底。不過，子類別中的 :meth:`!__init__` 方法需要呼"
"叫 :meth:`Handler.__init__`。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:524
msgid ""
"Initializes the :class:`Handler` instance by setting its level, setting the "
"list of filters to the empty list and creating a lock "
"(using :meth:`createLock`) for serializing access to an I/O mechanism."
msgstr ""
"初始化 :class:`Handler` 實例：設定其等級、將過濾器串列設為空串列，並（使"
"用 :meth:`createLock`）建立一個鎖，讓對 I/O 機制的存取能依序進行。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:531
msgid ""
"Initializes a thread lock which can be used to serialize access to "
"underlying I/O functionality which may not be threadsafe."
msgstr ""
"初始化一個執行緒鎖，可用來讓對底層 I/O 功能（可能不是執行緒安全的）的存取依序"
"進行。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:537
msgid "Acquires the thread lock created with :meth:`createLock`."
msgstr "取得以 :meth:`createLock` 建立的執行緒鎖。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:542
msgid "Releases the thread lock acquired with :meth:`acquire`."
msgstr "釋放以 :meth:`acquire` 取得的執行緒鎖。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:547
msgid ""
"Sets the threshold for this handler to *level*. Logging messages which are "
"less severe than *level* will be ignored. When a handler is created, the "
"level is set to :const:`NOTSET` (which causes all messages to be processed)."
msgstr ""
"將此處理器的門檻設為 *level*。嚴重性低於 *level* 的日誌訊息會被忽略。建立處理"
"器時，等級會被設為 :const:`NOTSET`\\ （這會使所有訊息都被處理）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:554
msgid ""
"The *level* parameter now accepts a string representation of the level such "
"as 'INFO' as an alternative to the integer constants such as :const:`INFO`."
msgstr ""
"*level* 參數現在除了接受像 :const:`INFO` 這樣的整數常數外，也接受等級的字串表"
"示，例如 'INFO'。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:562
msgid ""
"Sets the formatter for this handler to *fmt*. The *fmt* argument must be "
"a :class:`Formatter` instance or ``None``."
msgstr ""
"將此處理器的格式化器設為 *fmt*。*fmt* 引數必須是 :class:`Formatter` 實例或 "
"``None``。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:568
msgid "Adds the specified filter *filter* to this handler."
msgstr "將指定的過濾器 *filter* 加入此處理器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:573
msgid "Removes the specified filter *filter* from this handler."
msgstr "從此處理器移除指定的過濾器 *filter*。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:578
msgid ""
"Apply this handler's filters to the record and return ``True`` if the record "
"is to be processed. The filters are consulted in turn, until one of them "
"returns a false value. If none of them return a false value, the record will "
"be emitted. If one returns a false value, the handler will not emit the "
"record."
msgstr ""
"將此處理器的過濾器套用到紀錄上，若該紀錄要被處理則回傳 ``True``。過濾器會依序"
"被詢問，直到其中一個回傳假值為止。如果沒有任何過濾器回傳假值，該紀錄就會被發"
"出。如果有一個回傳假值，處理器就不會發出該紀錄。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:587
msgid ""
"Ensure all logging output has been flushed. This version does nothing and is "
"intended to be implemented by subclasses."
msgstr "確保所有日誌輸出都已排清 (flush)。此版本不做任何事，預期由子類別實作。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:593
msgid ""
"Tidy up any resources used by the handler. This version does no output but "
"removes the handler from an internal map of handlers, which is used for "
"handler lookup by name."
msgstr ""
"清理處理器所使用的所有資源。此版本不會產生輸出，但會從處理器的內部對映中移除"
"此處理器，該對映是用來依名稱查找處理器的。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:597
msgid ""
"Subclasses should ensure that this gets called from overridden :meth:`close` "
"methods."
msgstr "子類別應確保在覆寫的 :meth:`close` 方法中會呼叫此方法。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:603
msgid ""
"Conditionally emits the specified logging record, depending on filters which "
"may have been added to the handler. Wraps the actual emission of the record "
"with acquisition/release of the I/O thread lock."
msgstr ""
"根據可能已加入處理器的過濾器，有條件地發出指定的日誌紀錄。在實際發出紀錄的前"
"後，會取得／釋放 I/O 執行緒鎖。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:610
msgid ""
"This method should be called from handlers when an exception is encountered "
"during an :meth:`emit` call. If the module-level "
"attribute :data:`raiseExceptions` is ``False``, exceptions get silently "
"ignored. This is what is mostly wanted for a logging system - most users "
"will not care about errors in the logging system, they are more interested "
"in application errors. You could, however, replace this with a custom "
"handler if you wish. The specified record is the one which was being "
"processed when the exception occurred. (The default value "
"of :data:`raiseExceptions` is ``True``, as that is more useful during "
"development)."
msgstr ""
"當處理器在 :meth:`emit` 呼叫期間遇到例外時，應呼叫此方法。如果模組層級屬"
"性 :data:`raiseExceptions` 為 ``False``，例外會被默默忽略。這通常正是日誌記錄"
"系統所需要的行為：大多數使用者不會在意日誌記錄系統中的錯誤，他們更關心的是應"
"用程式的錯誤。不過，如果你願意，也可以用自訂的錯誤處理方法取代此方法。所指定"
"的紀錄是例外發生時正在處理的那筆紀錄。（:data:`raiseExceptions` 的預設值為 "
"``True``，因為這在開發期間比較有用。）"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:623
msgid ""
"Do formatting for a record - if a formatter is set, use it. Otherwise, use "
"the default formatter for the module."
msgstr ""
"對紀錄進行格式化：如果有設定格式化器就使用它，否則使用模組的預設格式化器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:629
msgid ""
"Do whatever it takes to actually log the specified logging record. This "
"version is intended to be implemented by subclasses and so raises "
"a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"執行實際記錄指定日誌紀錄所需的一切工作。此版本預期由子類別實作，因此會引"
"發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:633
msgid ""
"This method is called after a handler-level lock is acquired, which is "
"released after this method returns. When you override this method, note that "
"you should be careful when calling anything that invokes other parts of the "
"logging API which might do locking, because that might result in a deadlock. "
"Specifically:"
msgstr ""
"此方法會在取得處理器層級的鎖之後被呼叫，該鎖會在此方法回傳後釋放。覆寫此方法"
"時請注意，呼叫任何會叫用日誌記錄 API 其他部分（可能會進行鎖定）的東西時都要小"
"心，因為這可能導致死鎖。具體來說："

#: ../../library/logging.rst:639
msgid ""
"Logging configuration APIs acquire the module-level lock, and then "
"individual handler-level locks as those handlers are configured."
msgstr ""
"日誌設定 API 會先取得模組層級的鎖，接著在設定各個處理器時取得個別處理器層級的"
"鎖。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:642
msgid ""
"Many logging APIs lock the module-level lock. If such an API is called from "
"this method, it could cause a deadlock if a configuration call is made on "
"another thread, because that thread will try to acquire the module-level "
"lock *before* the handler-level lock, whereas this thread tries to acquire "
"the module-level lock *after* the handler-level lock (because in this "
"method, the handler-level lock has already been acquired)."
msgstr ""
"許多日誌記錄 API 會鎖定模組層級的鎖。如果從此方法中呼叫這樣的 API，而另一個執"
"行緒正在進行設定呼叫，就可能造成死鎖，因為那個執行緒會嘗試在處理器層級的鎖\\ "
"*之前*\\ 取得模組層級的鎖，而此執行緒則是嘗試在處理器層級的鎖\\ *之後*\\ 才取"
"得模組層級的鎖（因為在此方法中，處理器層級的鎖已經被取得了）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:649
msgid ""
"For a list of handlers included as standard, see :mod:`logging.handlers`."
msgstr "標準內建的處理器清單請參閱 :mod:`logging.handlers`。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:654
msgid "Formatter Objects"
msgstr "Formatter 物件"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:660
msgid ""
"Responsible for converting a :class:`LogRecord` to an output string to be "
"interpreted by a human or external system."
msgstr "負責將 :class:`LogRecord` 轉換為供人類或外部系統解讀的輸出字串。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "參數"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:663
msgid ""
"A format string in the given *style* for the logged output as a whole. The "
"possible mapping keys are drawn from the :class:`LogRecord` "
"object's :ref:`logrecord-attributes`. If not specified, ``'%(message)s'`` is "
"used, which is just the logged message."
msgstr ""
"以指定的 *style* 撰寫、用於整個日誌輸出的格式字串。可用的對映鍵取"
"自 :class:`LogRecord` 物件的 :ref:`logrecord-attributes`。若未指定，則會使用 "
"``'%(message)s'``，也就是只有所記錄的訊息。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:671
msgid ""
"A format string for the date/time portion of the logged output. If not "
"specified, the default described in :meth:`formatTime` is used."
msgstr ""
"用於日誌輸出中日期／時間部分的格式字串。若未指定，則會使"
"用 :meth:`formatTime` 中所描述的預設值。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:675
msgid ""
"Can be one of ``'%'``, ``'{'`` or ``'$'`` and determines how the format "
"string will be merged with its data: using one of :ref:`old-string-"
"formatting` (``%``), :meth:`str.format` (``{``) or :class:`string.Template` "
"(``$``). This only applies to *fmt* (e.g. ``'%(message)s'`` versus "
"``'{message}'``), not to the actual log messages passed to the logging "
"methods. However, there are :ref:`other ways <formatting-styles>` to use "
"``{``- and ``$``-formatting for log messages."
msgstr ""
"可以是 ``'%'``、``'{'`` 或 ``'$'`` 其中之一，決定格式字串要如何與其資料合併："
"分別使用 :ref:`old-string-formatting` (``%``)、:meth:`str.format` (``{``) "
"或 :class:`string.Template` (``$``)。這只適用於 *fmt*\\ （例如 ``'%"
"(message)s'`` 與 ``'{message}'``），而不適用於傳給日誌記錄方法的實際日誌訊"
"息。不過，還是有\\ :ref:`其他方式 <formatting-styles>`\\ 可以對日誌訊息使用 "
"``{`` 和 ``$`` 格式化。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:685
msgid ""
"If ``True`` (the default), incorrect or mismatched *fmt* and *style* will "
"raise a :exc:`ValueError`; for example, ``logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %"
"(message)s', style='{')``."
msgstr ""
"若為 ``True``\\ （預設值），不正確或不相符的 *fmt* 與 *style* 會引"
"發 :exc:`ValueError`；例如 ``logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %(message)s', "
"style='{')``。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:690
msgid ""
"A dictionary with default values to use in custom fields. For example, "
"``logging.Formatter('%(ip)s %(message)s', defaults={\"ip\": None})``"
msgstr ""
"一個字典，包含要用於自訂欄位的預設值。例如 ``logging.Formatter('%(ip)s %"
"(message)s', defaults={\"ip\": None})``"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:695
msgid "Added the *style* parameter."
msgstr "新增 *style* 參數。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:698
msgid "Added the *validate* parameter."
msgstr "新增 *validate* 參數。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:701
msgid "Added the *defaults* parameter."
msgstr "新增 *defaults* 參數。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:707
msgid ""
"The record's attribute dictionary is used as the operand to a string "
"formatting operation. Returns the resulting string. Before formatting the "
"dictionary, a couple of preparatory steps are carried out. The *message* "
"attribute of the record is computed using *msg* % *args*. If the formatting "
"string contains ``'(asctime)'``, :meth:`formatTime` is called to format the "
"event time. If there is exception information, it is formatted "
"using :meth:`formatException` and appended to the message. Note that the "
"formatted exception information is cached in attribute *exc_text*. This is "
"useful because the exception information can be pickled and sent across the "
"wire, but you should be careful if you have more than one :class:`Formatter` "
"subclass which customizes the formatting of exception information. In this "
"case, you will have to clear the cached value (by setting the *exc_text* "
"attribute to ``None``) after a formatter has done its formatting, so that "
"the next formatter to handle the event doesn't use the cached value, but "
"recalculates it afresh."
msgstr ""
"紀錄的屬性字典會被用作字串格式化操作的運算元。回傳結果字串。在格式化字典之"
"前，會先執行幾個準備步驟。紀錄的 *message* 屬性是以 *msg* % *args* 計算而得。"
"如果格式字串包含 ``'(asctime)'``，就會呼叫 :meth:`formatTime` 來格式化事件時"
"間。如果有例外資訊，就會使用 :meth:`formatException` 將其格式化並附加到訊息後"
"面。請注意，格式化後的例外資訊會快取在 *exc_text* 屬性中。這很有用，因為例外"
"資訊可以被 pickle 並透過網路傳送，但如果你有多個會自訂例外資訊格式"
"的 :class:`Formatter` 子類別，就要特別小心。在這種情況下，你必須在格式化器完"
"成格式化後清除快取的值（將 *exc_text* 屬性設為 ``None``），這樣下一個處理該事"
"件的格式化器才不會使用快取的值，而是重新計算。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:723
msgid ""
"If stack information is available, it's appended after the exception "
"information, using :meth:`formatStack` to transform it if necessary."
msgstr ""
"如果有堆疊資訊，會將其附加在例外資訊之後，必要時會使用 :meth:`formatStack` 進"
"行轉換。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:729
msgid ""
"This method should be called from :meth:`format` by a formatter which wants "
"to make use of a formatted time. This method can be overridden in formatters "
"to provide for any specific requirement, but the basic behavior is as "
"follows: if *datefmt* (a string) is specified, it is used "
"with :func:`time.strftime` to format the creation time of the record. "
"Otherwise, the format '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S,uuu' is used, where the uuu part is "
"a millisecond value and the other letters are as per "
"the :func:`time.strftime` documentation.  An example time in this format is "
"``2003-01-23 00:29:50,411``.  The resulting string is returned."
msgstr ""
"想要使用格式化時間的格式化器，應從 :meth:`format` 中呼叫此方法。可以在格式化"
"器中覆寫此方法以滿足任何特定需求，但基本行為如下：如果有指定 *datefmt*\\ （一"
"個字串），就會將它與 :func:`time.strftime` 搭配使用來格式化紀錄的建立時間。否"
"則會使用格式 '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S,uuu'，其中 uuu 部分是毫秒值，其他字母則依"
"照 :func:`time.strftime` 文件的定義。此格式的時間範例為 ``2003-01-23 "
"00:29:50,411``。回傳結果字串。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:739
msgid ""
"This function uses a user-configurable function to convert the creation time "
"to a tuple. By default, :func:`time.localtime` is used; to change this for a "
"particular formatter instance, set the ``converter`` attribute to a function "
"with the same signature as :func:`time.localtime` or :func:`time.gmtime`. To "
"change it for all formatters, for example if you want all logging times to "
"be shown in GMT, set the ``converter`` attribute in the ``Formatter`` class."
msgstr ""
"此函式使用一個可由使用者設定的函式，將建立時間轉換為元組。預設使"
"用 :func:`time.localtime`；如果要針對特定格式化器實例更改此設定，請將 "
"``converter`` 屬性設為與 :func:`time.localtime` 或 :func:`time.gmtime` 具有相"
"同簽名的函式。如果要更改所有格式化器的設定，例如想讓所有日誌時間都以 GMT 顯"
"示，請在 ``Formatter`` 類別中設定 ``converter`` 屬性。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:747
msgid ""
"Previously, the default format was hard-coded as in this example: "
"``2010-09-06 22:38:15,292`` where the part before the comma is handled by a "
"strftime format string (``'%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'``), and the part after the "
"comma is a millisecond value. Because strftime does not have a format "
"placeholder for milliseconds, the millisecond value is appended using "
"another format string, ``'%s,%03d'`` --- and both of these format strings "
"have been hardcoded into this method. With the change, these strings are "
"defined as class-level attributes which can be overridden at the instance "
"level when desired. The names of the attributes are ``default_time_format`` "
"(for the strftime format string) and ``default_msec_format`` (for appending "
"the millisecond value)."
msgstr ""
"先前，預設格式是寫死的，如此範例：``2010-09-06 22:38:15,292``，其中逗號前的部"
"分由 strftime 格式字串 (``'%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'``) 處理，逗號後的部分則是毫秒"
"值。由於 strftime 沒有毫秒的格式佔位符號，因此毫秒值是使用另一個格式字串 "
"``'%s,%03d'`` 附加上去的 --- 而這兩個格式字串都被寫死在此方法中。經過這次變更"
"後，這些字串被定義為類別層級的屬性，需要時可以在實例層級覆寫。這些屬性的名稱"
"為 ``default_time_format``\\ （用於 strftime 格式字串）和 "
"``default_msec_format``\\ （用於附加毫秒值）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:760
msgid "The ``default_msec_format`` can be ``None``."
msgstr "``default_msec_format`` 可以是 ``None``。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:765
msgid ""
"Formats the specified exception information (a standard exception tuple as "
"returned by :func:`sys.exc_info`) as a string. This default implementation "
"just uses :func:`traceback.print_exception`. The resulting string is "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"將指定的例外資訊（由 :func:`sys.exc_info` 回傳的標準例外元組）格式化為字串。"
"此預設實作僅使用 :func:`traceback.print_exception`。回傳結果字串。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:772
msgid ""
"Formats the specified stack information (a string as returned "
"by :func:`traceback.print_stack`, but with the last newline removed) as a "
"string. This default implementation just returns the input value."
msgstr ""
"將指定的堆疊資訊（由 :func:`traceback.print_stack` 回傳、但移除了最後一個換行"
"字元的字串）格式化為字串。此預設實作只會回傳輸入值。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:778
msgid ""
"A base formatter class suitable for subclassing when you want to format a "
"number of records. You can pass a :class:`Formatter` instance which you want "
"to use to format each line (that corresponds to a single record). If not "
"specified, the default formatter (which just outputs the event message) is "
"used as the line formatter."
msgstr ""
"一個基底格式化器類別，適合在你想要格式化多筆紀錄時作為子類別化的基礎。你可以"
"傳入一個 :class:`Formatter` 實例，用來格式化每一列（對應單一紀錄）。若未指"
"定，則會使用預設格式化器（只輸出事件訊息）作為列格式化器。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:786
msgid ""
"Return a header for a list of *records*. The base implementation just "
"returns the empty string. You will need to override this method if you want "
"specific behaviour, e.g. to show the count of records, a title or a "
"separator line."
msgstr ""
"回傳 *records* 串列的標頭。基底實作只會回傳空字串。如果你想要特定的行為，例如"
"顯示紀錄數量、標題或分隔線，就需要覆寫此方法。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:793
msgid ""
"Return a footer for a list of *records*. The base implementation just "
"returns the empty string. You will need to override this method if you want "
"specific behaviour, e.g. to show the count of records or a separator line."
msgstr ""
"回傳 *records* 串列的結尾。基底實作只會回傳空字串。如果你想要特定的行為，例如"
"顯示紀錄數量或分隔線，就需要覆寫此方法。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:800
msgid ""
"Return formatted text for a list of *records*. The base implementation just "
"returns the empty string if there are no records; otherwise, it returns the "
"concatenation of the header, each record formatted with the line formatter, "
"and the footer."
msgstr ""
"回傳 *records* 串列格式化後的文字。如果沒有任何紀錄，基底實作只會回傳空字串；"
"否則會回傳由標頭、以列格式化器格式化的每筆紀錄，以及結尾串接而成的結果。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:808
msgid "Filter Objects"
msgstr "Filter 物件"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:810
msgid ""
"``Filters`` can be used by ``Handlers`` and ``Loggers`` for more "
"sophisticated filtering than is provided by levels. The base filter class "
"only allows events which are below a certain point in the logger hierarchy. "
"For example, a filter initialized with 'A.B' will allow events logged by "
"loggers 'A.B', 'A.B.C', 'A.B.C.D', 'A.B.D' etc. but not 'A.BB', 'B.A.B' etc. "
"If initialized with the empty string, all events are passed."
msgstr ""
"``Handlers`` 和 ``Loggers`` 可以使用 ``Filters`` 來進行比等級更精細的過濾。基"
"底過濾器類別只允許記錄器階層中位於某個點以下的事件通過。例如，以 'A.B' 初始化"
"的過濾器會允許記錄器 'A.B'、'A.B.C'、'A.B.C.D'、'A.B.D' 等所記錄的事件，但不"
"允許 'A.BB'、'B.A.B' 等。如果以空字串初始化，則所有事件都會通過。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:820
msgid ""
"Returns an instance of the :class:`Filter` class. If *name* is specified, it "
"names a logger which, together with its children, will have its events "
"allowed through the filter. If *name* is the empty string, allows every "
"event."
msgstr ""
"回傳 :class:`Filter` 類別的實例。如果有指定 *name*，它指的是一個記錄器，該記"
"錄器及其子記錄器的事件將被允許通過過濾器。如果 *name* 為空字串，則允許所有事"
"件。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:827
msgid ""
"Is the specified record to be logged? Returns false for no, true for yes. "
"Filters can either modify log records in-place or return a completely "
"different record instance which will replace the original log record in any "
"future processing of the event."
msgstr ""
"指定的紀錄是否要被記錄？回傳 false 表示否，true 表示是。過濾器可以原地修改日"
"誌紀錄，也可以回傳一個完全不同的紀錄實例，在該事件後續的所有處理中取代原本的"
"日誌紀錄。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:832
msgid ""
"Note that filters attached to handlers are consulted before an event is "
"emitted by the handler, whereas filters attached to loggers are consulted "
"whenever an event is logged (using :meth:`debug`, :meth:`info`, etc.), "
"before sending an event to handlers. This means that events which have been "
"generated by descendant loggers will not be filtered by a logger's filter "
"setting, unless the filter has also been applied to those descendant loggers."
msgstr ""
"請注意，附加在處理器上的過濾器會在處理器發出事件之前被詢問，而附加在記錄器上"
"的過濾器則會在每次記錄事件時（使用 :meth:`debug`、:meth:`info` 等）、將事件傳"
"送給處理器之前被詢問。這表示由後代記錄器產生的事件不會被某個記錄器的過濾器設"
"定所過濾，除非該過濾器也被套用到那些後代記錄器上。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:839
msgid ""
"You don't actually need to subclass ``Filter``: you can pass any instance "
"which has a ``filter`` method with the same semantics."
msgstr ""
"你其實不需要建立 ``Filter`` 的子類別：你可以傳入任何具有相同語意之 "
"``filter`` 方法的實例。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:842
msgid ""
"You don't need to create specialized ``Filter`` classes, or use other "
"classes with a ``filter`` method: you can use a function (or other callable) "
"as a filter. The filtering logic will check to see if the filter object has "
"a ``filter`` attribute: if it does, it's assumed to be a ``Filter`` and "
"its :meth:`~Filter.filter` method is called. Otherwise, it's assumed to be a "
"callable and called with the record as the single parameter. The returned "
"value should conform to that returned by :meth:`~Filter.filter`."
msgstr ""
"你不需要建立特製的 ``Filter`` 類別，也不需要使用其他具有 ``filter`` 方法的類"
"別：你可以使用函式（或其他可呼叫物件）作為過濾器。過濾邏輯會檢查過濾器物件是"
"否具有 ``filter`` 屬性：如果有，就假定它是 ``Filter`` 並呼叫"
"其 :meth:`~Filter.filter` 方法；否則就假定它是可呼叫物件，並以該紀錄作為唯一"
"參數來呼叫它。回傳值應與 :meth:`~Filter.filter` 的回傳值一致。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:852
msgid ""
"You can now return a :class:`LogRecord` instance from filters to replace the "
"log record rather than modifying it in place. This allows filters attached "
"to a :class:`Handler` to modify the log record before it is emitted, without "
"having side effects on other handlers."
msgstr ""
"現在你可以從過濾器回傳一個 :class:`LogRecord` 實例來取代日誌紀錄，而不是原地"
"修改它。這讓附加在 :class:`Handler` 上的過濾器可以在日誌紀錄被發出之前修改"
"它，而不會對其他處理器產生副作用。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:858
msgid ""
"Although filters are used primarily to filter records based on more "
"sophisticated criteria than levels, they get to see every record which is "
"processed by the handler or logger they're attached to: this can be useful "
"if you want to do things like counting how many records were processed by a "
"particular logger or handler, or adding, changing or removing attributes in "
"the :class:`LogRecord` being processed. Obviously changing the LogRecord "
"needs to be done with some care, but it does allow the injection of "
"contextual information into logs (see :ref:`filters-contextual`)."
msgstr ""
"雖然過濾器主要用來根據比等級更精細的條件來過濾紀錄，但它們能看到所附加的處理"
"器或記錄器所處理的每一筆紀錄：如果你想做一些事情，例如計算特定記錄器或處理器"
"處理了多少筆紀錄，或是在正在處理的 :class:`LogRecord` 中新增、變更或移除屬"
"性，這就很有用。顯然，變更 LogRecord 時需要小心，但這確實能將情境資訊注入日誌"
"中（請參閱 :ref:`filters-contextual`）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:871
msgid "LogRecord Objects"
msgstr "LogRecord 物件"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:873
msgid ""
":class:`LogRecord` instances are created automatically by "
"the :class:`Logger` every time something is logged, and can be created "
"manually via :func:`makeLogRecord` (for example, from a pickled event "
"received over the wire)."
msgstr ""
"每次記錄某些內容時，:class:`Logger` 都會自動建立 :class:`LogRecord` 實例，也"
"可以透過 :func:`makeLogRecord` 手動建立（例如從透過網路接收、經 pickle 的事件"
"建立）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:881
msgid "Contains all the information pertinent to the event being logged."
msgstr "包含與正在記錄之事件相關的所有資訊。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:883
msgid ""
"The primary information is passed in *msg* and *args*, which are combined "
"using ``msg % args`` to create the :attr:`!message` attribute of the record."
msgstr ""
"主要資訊透過 *msg* 和 *args* 傳入，兩者會使用 ``msg % args`` 結合，以建立紀錄"
"的 :attr:`!message` 屬性。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:887
msgid ""
"The name of the logger used to log the event represented by this :class:`!"
"LogRecord`. Note that the logger name in the :class:`!LogRecord` will always "
"have this value, even though it may be emitted by a handler attached to a "
"different (ancestor) logger."
msgstr ""
"用來記錄此 :class:`!LogRecord` 所代表之事件的記錄器名稱。請注意，:class:`!"
"LogRecord` 中的記錄器名稱一律會是這個值，即使它可能是由附加在另一個（上層）記"
"錄器上的處理器所發出的。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:895
msgid ""
"The :ref:`numeric level <levels>` of the logging event (such as ``10`` for "
"``DEBUG``, ``20`` for ``INFO``, etc). Note that this is converted to *two* "
"attributes of the LogRecord: :attr:`!levelno` for the numeric value "
"and :attr:`!levelname` for the corresponding level name."
msgstr ""
"日誌事件的\\ :ref:`數值等級 <levels>`\\ （例如 ``DEBUG`` 為 ``10``、``INFO`` "
"為 ``20`` 等）。請注意，這會被轉換為 LogRecord 的\\ *兩個*\\ 屬性：數值"
"的 :attr:`!levelno` 和對應等級名稱的 :attr:`!levelname`。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:902
msgid ""
"The full string path of the source file where the logging call was made."
msgstr "進行日誌記錄呼叫之原始檔的完整路徑字串。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:906
msgid "The line number in the source file where the logging call was made."
msgstr "原始檔中進行日誌記錄呼叫的列號。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:910
msgid ""
"The event description message, which can be a %-format string with "
"placeholders for variable data, or an arbitrary object (see :ref:`arbitrary-"
"object-messages`)."
msgstr ""
"事件描述訊息，可以是帶有變數資料佔位符號的 % 格式字串，或是任意物件（請參"
"閱 :ref:`arbitrary-object-messages`）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:915
msgid ""
"Variable data to merge into the *msg* argument to obtain the event "
"description."
msgstr "要合併到 *msg* 引數中以取得事件描述的變數資料。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:919
msgid ""
"An exception tuple with the current exception information, as returned "
"by :func:`sys.exc_info`, or ``None`` if no exception information is "
"available."
msgstr ""
"一個包含目前例外資訊的例外元組（如 :func:`sys.exc_info` 所回傳），若沒有可用"
"的例外資訊則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:924
msgid ""
"The name of the function or method from which the logging call was invoked."
msgstr "發起日誌記錄呼叫的函式或方法名稱。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:928
msgid ""
"A text string representing stack information from the base of the stack in "
"the current thread, up to the logging call."
msgstr "一個文字字串，表示目前執行緒中從堆疊底部到日誌記錄呼叫為止的堆疊資訊。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:935
msgid ""
"Returns the message for this :class:`LogRecord` instance after merging any "
"user-supplied arguments with the message. If the user-supplied message "
"argument to the logging call is not a string, :func:`str` is called on it to "
"convert it to a string. This allows use of user-defined classes as messages, "
"whose ``__str__`` method can return the actual format string to be used."
msgstr ""
"將使用者提供的引數與訊息合併後，回傳此 :class:`LogRecord` 實例的訊息。如果使"
"用者傳給日誌記錄呼叫的訊息引數不是字串，就會對它呼叫 :func:`str` 以將其轉換為"
"字串。這讓使用者定義的類別可以作為訊息使用，其 ``__str__`` 方法可以回傳實際要"
"使用的格式字串。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:942
msgid ""
"The creation of a :class:`LogRecord` has been made more configurable by "
"providing a factory which is used to create the record. The factory can be "
"set using :func:`getLogRecordFactory` and :func:`setLogRecordFactory` (see "
"this for the factory's signature)."
msgstr ""
"藉由提供一個用來建立紀錄的工廠，:class:`LogRecord` 的建立方式變得更可自訂。可"
"以使用 :func:`getLogRecordFactory` 和 :func:`setLogRecordFactory` 來設定該工"
"廠（工廠的簽名請參閱後者）。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:948
msgid ""
"This functionality can be used to inject your own values into "
"a :class:`LogRecord` at creation time. You can use the following pattern::"
msgstr ""
"此功能可用來在建立 :class:`LogRecord` 時注入你自己的值。你可以使用以下模"
"式： ::"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:951
msgid ""
"old_factory = logging.getLogRecordFactory()\n"
"\n"
"def record_factory(*args, **kwargs):\n"
"    record = old_factory(*args, **kwargs)\n"
"    record.custom_attribute = 0xdecafbad\n"
"    return record\n"
"\n"
"logging.setLogRecordFactory(record_factory)"
msgstr ""
"old_factory = logging.getLogRecordFactory()\n"
"\n"
"def record_factory(*args, **kwargs):\n"
"    record = old_factory(*args, **kwargs)\n"
"    record.custom_attribute = 0xdecafbad\n"
"    return record\n"
"\n"
"logging.setLogRecordFactory(record_factory)"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:960
msgid ""
"With this pattern, multiple factories could be chained, and as long as they "
"don't overwrite each other's attributes or unintentionally overwrite the "
"standard attributes listed above, there should be no surprises."
msgstr ""
"使用這種模式，可以將多個工廠串接起來，只要它們不會覆寫彼此的屬性，或無意間覆"
"寫上面列出的標準屬性，應該就不會有意外狀況。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:969
msgid "LogRecord attributes"
msgstr "LogRecord 屬性"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:971
msgid ""
"The LogRecord has a number of attributes, most of which are derived from the "
"parameters to the constructor. (Note that the names do not always correspond "
"exactly between the LogRecord constructor parameters and the LogRecord "
"attributes.) These attributes can be used to merge data from the record into "
"the format string. The following table lists (in alphabetical order) the "
"attribute names, their meanings and the corresponding placeholder in a %-"
"style format string."
msgstr ""
"LogRecord 有許多屬性，其中大部分衍生自建構函式的參數。（請注意，LogRecord 建"
"構函式參數與 LogRecord 屬性之間的名稱並不總是完全對應。）這些屬性可用來將紀錄"
"中的資料合併到格式字串中。下表（依字母順序）列出了屬性名稱、其意義，以及在 % "
"風格格式字串中對應的佔位符號。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:979
msgid ""
"If you are using {}-formatting (:func:`str.format`), you can use ``{attrname}"
"`` as the placeholder in the format string. If you are using $-formatting "
"(:class:`string.Template`), use the form ``${attrname}``. In both cases, of "
"course, replace ``attrname`` with the actual attribute name you want to use."
msgstr ""
"如果你使用 {} 格式化 (:func:`str.format`)，可以在格式字串中使用 ``{attrname}"
"`` 作為佔位符號。如果你使用 $ 格式化 (:class:`string.Template`)，請使用 ``$"
"{attrname}`` 的形式。當然，在這兩種情況下，都要將 ``attrname`` 替換為你想使用"
"的實際屬性名稱。"

#: ../../library/logging.rst:985
msgid ""
"In the case of {}-formatting, you can specify formatting flags by placing "
"them after the attribute name, separated from it with a colon. For example: "
"a placeholder of ``{msecs:03.0f}`` would format a millisecond value of ``4`` "
"as ``004``. Refer to the :meth:`str.format` documentation for full details "
"on the options available to you."
msgstr ""
"在 {} 格式化的情況下，你可以藉由將格式化旗標放在屬性名稱之後（並以冒號與其分"
"隔）來指定它們。例如：佔位符號 ``{msecs:03.0f}`` 會將毫秒值 ``4`` 格式化為 "
"``004``。關於可用選項的完整細節，請參閱 :meth:`str.format` 的文件。"

